        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊ — munisiko — \"to sulk\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತಿಂಡಿ ಸಿಗಲಿಲ್ಲ ಅಂತ ತಂಗಿ ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊಂಡಳು. tiṇḍi sigalilla anta taṅgi munisikoṇḍaḷu. My little sister sulked because she did not get a snack."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊಂಡೆ, munisikoṇḍe."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With whom: … ಮೇಲೆ ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊ (munisiko). ಮುನಿಸು is a sulk."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುನಿಸಿಕೊ (munisiko) is native Dravidian: DEDR 5021 lists Kannada muni, \"to become angry\", and munisu, \"anger\"; -ko adds \"for oneself\", so the anger is turned inward."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
