              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುಗುಳ್ನಗು — muguḷnagu — \"to smile\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಳೆಯ ಫೋಟೋ ನೋಡಿ ಅಜ್ಜಿ ಮುಗುಳ್ನಕ್ಕರು. haḷeya phōṭō nōḍi ajji muguḷnakkaru. Looking at the old photo, grandmother smiled."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮುಗುಳ್ನಕ್ಕೆ, muguḷnakke."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುಗುಳು, a bud + ನಗು, to laugh: a laugh still in the bud. The noun is ಮುಗುಳ್ನಗೆ, a smile."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುಗುಳ್ನಗು (muguḷnagu) is a native Dravidian compound: muguḷ, \"a bud; to close like a bud\" (DEDR 4893), and nagu, \"to laugh\" (DEDR 3569)."
            }
          ]
        },
